ut diagonalizing it, but the construction fails for the complex, non-normal Green's matrix G of an open scattering array of electric dipoles. We propose three real-valued, positive landscapes built from the Feinberg--Zee hermitization of G: a regularised Gramian inverse (Gram), the diagonal Schur block that</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bed399acb18f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:08:22 GMT</pubDate><source>arXiv 光学与光子学 (physics.optics)</source><category>科研进展</category></item><item><title>Solid-state emissive acceptors enable thermally accessible radiative pathways for efficient organic solar cells</title><link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41566-026-02009-8</link><description>Nature Photonics, Published online: 12 October 2026; doi:10.1038/s41566-026-02009-8 Solid-state emissive guest acceptors enhance organic solar cells by establishing thermally accessible radiative pathways, significantly reducing non-radiative voltage loss end enabling ternary blend devices with a certified power conversion efficiency of 20.84%.</description><guid isPermaLink="false">497d2a439e28</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:08:22 GMT</pubDate><source>Nature Photonics</source><category>光伏与新能源</category></item></channel></rss>